      "prior_exception": {
        "type": "no-defensible-ucr-match",
        "reason": "The Radboud degree is an integrated molecular biology AND chemistry programme. Its compulsory first year already includes atoms and molecules, analytical chemistry and a chemical-analysis lab, organic chemistry and synthesis lab, biochemistry and its lab, thermodynamics, cell biophysics and a molecular-sciences lab. The later compulsory core deepens organic, inorganic and analytical chemistry, crystal structure, biomolecular mechanisms and structural bioinformatics, then requires a supervised 12-EC research internship. UCR offers valuable molecular-cell and biomedical courses but lacks a sequence in organic/inorganic/analytical/physical chemistry, molecular spectroscopy and synthesis, and has only one broad life-science laboratory course. A 24-course UCR schedule could sustain biomedical biology with data methods, but it would omit the defining chemistry and multi-lab spine and would misrepresent equivalence to this molecular-science degree.",
        "checkedOn": "2026-09-25",
        "curriculumContext": "The current adopted 2026–27 Faculty of Science EER, rather than the loosely grouped prospective year-three thematic examples, controls the 180-EC reconstruction. Its differentiation phase is restricted and its research internship is mandatory. The exception follows assessment of the closest 24-course molecular/biomedical possibility against the entire current UCR enriched course database.",
        "ucrCourseEvidence": "Read all 151 current enriched UCR course rows with descriptions, profiles, semester availability and prerequisites. HCBGATE101 Foundation of Life, Health & Biomedicine, HCBLIFE211 Molecular Cell Biology, HCBLIFE213 Biochemistry, HCBLIFE214 Life Science Laboratory, HCBLIFE311 Molecular Pathology & Genetics and HCBBIOM312 Infection & Immunity cover genuine biological and biomedical parts. DISGATE101 Introduction to Programming, DISGATE102 Mathematical Methods, DISDATA111 Introduction to Data Science and BENGATE102 Research Methods & Statistics can support quantitative work. HCBLIFE214 introduces biochemical and molecular lab techniques, but no available courses provide the formally required analytical-chemistry lab, organic synthesis laboratories, physical chemistry/thermodynamics, spectroscopy or a sustained organic/inorganic chemistry progression. The only feasible alternative would be a different biomedical/data curriculum, so no 24-course closest UCR degree is encoded."
      },
